      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-46958",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/85/85e0e81c89f5f2a3b47e1fa22ded61467cca9e468823f55832891f72763ffc0d.png)\n\nJohn surveyed the children from Jefferson Elementary School to determine their favorite pets. The diagram above shows the results of his survey.\n\nThere are $120$ students at Little Harbor Elementary School. Assuming that the distribution of favorite pets is the same in both schools, find the number of children who prefer parrots at Little Harbor Elementary School.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
